Ah, I apologize! Thank you for clarifying that it is specifically the **"Download Batch"** button.
I know exactly why this is happening. In your DialogContent, the "Download Batch" button is the **very first actual <Button> element** in the DOM tree.
Material UI (MUI) has a built-in accessibility feature called a **"Focus Trap"**. When a user clicks dead space inside a dialog or clicks the backdrop, MUI panics and thinks, *"The user lost their place! I need to throw the focus onto the first button I can find!"* Because "Download Batch" is the first button, it gets hit with a "ghost focus," making it look highlighted.
Here are the two exact steps to stop MUI from forcing focus onto that button.
### 1. Disable the Dialog's Aggressive Focus Trap
You need to tell the Dialog component that holds your View Modal to stop enforcing focus when the user clicks around.
Find your isViewModalOpen Dialog (around line 737) and add these three specific disable properties:
```jsx
        {/* --- View Details Modal --- */}
        <Dialog
          open={isViewModalOpen}
          onClose={handleCloseViewModal}
          fullWidth
          maxWidth="lg"
          disableAutoFocus={true}      // Prevents jumping to the first button on open
          disableEnforceFocus={true}   // Prevents forcing focus when clicking dead space
          disableRestoreFocus={true}   // Prevents ghost highlights when clicking outside
        >

```
### 2. Strip the Ghost Highlight from the Button
To be absolutely bulletproof, we can tell the "Download Batch" button to completely ignore the browser's attempt to force a "focus-visible" highlight ring on it, unless the user is explicitly hovering over it.
Find your Download Batch button (around line 943) and update its sx property to ignore the .Mui-focusVisible class:
```jsx
<Button 
  variant="outlined" 
  size="small" 
  startIcon={<FileDownloadIcon />} 
  onClick={handleDownloadExcel} 
  disabled={!viewingBatchId} 
  sx={{
    ...jaStyles.downloadBtn,
    // Kills the ghost highlight from MUI focus traps
    "&.Mui-focusVisible": {
      backgroundColor: "transparent",
      outline: "none",
      boxShadow: "none"
    },
    "&:focus": {
      outline: "none"
    }
  }}
>
  Download Batch
</Button>

```
### Why this instantly fixes it:
 1. By adding the disable... props to the <Dialog>, you stop the MUI engine from actively hunting for a button to highlight when the user clicks empty space.
 2. By adding the Mui-focusVisible override to the button, you guarantee that even if the browser tries to focus the button, it will remain visually normal and won't turn blue/gray.
Make those two quick additions and that annoying ghost highlight will be gone!
